## Initial Q&A
### Is there any official NASA policy, guideline, or documented practice that requires seeking blessings from the Pope or any religious authority before a space mission?
Answer: No, there is no official NASA policy, guideline, or documented practice that requires seeking blessings from the Pope or any religious authority before a space mission. The search result describes a Russian Orthodox blessing ritual that occurs at the Baikonur Cosmodrome in Kazakhstan, which NASA astronauts have participated in as a courtesy when launching on Russian Soyuz rockets, but this is a local tradition and not a NASA requirement.

Source URL: https://www.theverge.com/2015/4/1/8324707/astronauts-blessing-nasa-space-baikonur

### Has the Vatican (or any Pope in office) ever issued formal or public blessings specifically for NASA space missions?
Answer: Yes, the Vatican has issued blessings for NASA space missions on specific occasions, as documented by Pope Benedict XVI's 2011 live call to the space shuttle Endeavour and International Space Station crew, during which he gave a blessing and sent a silver medal into orbit, and Pope Paul VI's greeting sent with Apollo 11 in 1969. However, these appear to be isolated gestures rather than a formal or routine requirement for NASA missions.

Source URL: https://www.denverpost.com/2011/05/21/pope-blesses-astronauts-in-1st-papal-call-to-space-2/

### Are there any documented instances where NASA administrators or astronauts have sought and received papal blessings as part of mission preparations?
Answer: Yes, there is at least one documented instance where the Pope prayed for NASA astronauts, though it was a response to a crisis rather than a pre-mission blessing sought by NASA. During the Apollo 13 emergency in April 1970, Pope St. Paul VI publicly prayed for the crew's safety and later sent a congratulatory cable to President Nixon upon their safe return. However, this was not a formal part of mission preparations initiated by NASA, but rather a global and spiritual response to the perilous situation.

Source URL: https://www.ncregister.com/news/50-years-ago-the-pope-prayed-for-the-apollo-13-astronauts

